1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,532
Teacher midterm practice, question 28.

2
00:00:04,152 --> 00:00:09,622
True or false: the one zero zero family makes up the cube faces of the B C C

3
00:00:09,622 --> 00:00:14,886
unit cell, while for the F C C cell it is the one one zero family.

4
00:00:16,586 --> 00:00:21,092
A cube face cuts one axis at one and is parallel to the other two.

5
00:00:21,092 --> 00:00:25,659
That gives one zero zero, zero one zero, and zero zero one.

6
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:29,163
That is pure geometry of the cubic lattice.

7
00:00:29,163 --> 00:00:31,757
It does not depend on whether the extra atoms

8
00:00:31,757 --> 00:00:34,409
sit in the body center or on the faces.

9
00:00:35,029 --> 00:00:40,588
The one one zero planes cut diagonally through the cell. So the F C C part is wrong.

10
00:00:42,188 --> 00:00:44,084
So the answer is B: false.

11
00:00:44,904 --> 00:00:49,627
Miller indices describe the lattice geometry, not the arrangement of atoms in it.
